## 🌌 Research Overview

This division explores space science, aerospace engineering, spacecraft technologies, and the scientific investigation of the universe.

The goal is to understand the technologies that make space exploration possible and study the mysteries of the cosmos.

## 🔭 Research Areas

| Field | Focus |
|---|---|
| 🌌 Astronomy | Stars, planets, and galaxies |
| 🪐 Astrophysics | Physical processes in the universe |
| 🚀 Rocket Science | Propulsion and launch systems |
| 🛰️ Satellite Technology | Satellite design and systems |
| 🛸 Spacecraft Engineering | Spacecraft structures and control |
| 🌍 Planetary Science | Planets and their environments |
| 🌠 Cosmology | Origin and evolution of the universe |
| 📡 Space Communication | Communication beyond Earth |

## 🎯 Research Objectives

- Study astronomy and astrophysics fundamentals.
- Understand rocket propulsion principles.
- Explore satellite and spacecraft technologies.
- Investigate planetary environments.
- Learn orbital mechanics and space navigation.
- Explore future possibilities in space exploration.

## 🧪 Research & Simulations

Scientific investigations, calculations, and simulations will be documented here.

Each investigation should include:
- Research question
- Scientific background
- Mathematical models
- Methodology or simulation
- Results and observations
- Limitations and future questions

## 🛠️ Technologies & Tools

